"d307875a4d9989626102a07cd8863d6e3ec1dc4b","position":"1787468000754403001-5a77e082-1cb5-474c-af4d-22078366cc2c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"91d44a5489bd3244ba95a87412f8b89bb7a343b5d6a9fba63ae039a8d0eb7506","event_uuid":"4c591fa8-4a3a-4dec-a86f-9ef0fefe6d46","position":{"commit_sha":"958ad677bd4da17675c31c32eafe1975fcca07a0","position":"1787470527722324001-4c591fa8-4a3a-4dec-a86f-9ef0fefe6d46"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c949b5548513859ee8edf2531c2d07b5879934244f31b3997cae2064e3c05e0f","event_uuid":"bf3642f0-4407-46f5-a01f-7dceb3d9e2c3","position":{"commit_sha":"94544051eac9ace58eeb043546689139903d2cbb","position":"1787470550550860001-bf3642f0-4407-46f5-a01f-7dceb3d9e2c3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"FORCE_CLAIM: plan-review gate bypassed by user approval — no plan-review attestation was verified. Reason: \"plan-review PASSED (REVIEW_RESULT sidecar records verdict PASS, 0 blocking/0 advisory) but attestation persistence lost the tracker-head race on every attempt (signing starvation under continuous multi-agent tracker write load; same failure signature as 3235-8aaf); operator-directed signing-starvation remediation\".","timestamp":1787456924821491001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"EVIDENCE OF COMPLETION — merged.\n\nChange: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2145 (LLM-Review+1, Verified+1, submitted; merged as ec028f59bd on main).\n\nWhat landed: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_dedup_seam_crossing.py — the seam-crossing dedup test with NO seeded invariants: the transport return comes from the REAL acli_cli_ops.add_comment (stubbed only at the _run_acli subprocess seam) fed the RECORDED ACLI batch envelope; recording via the REAL _record_comment_id against a REAL BindingStore; re-diff via the REAL _diff_comments on that SAME store. Jira-side body diverges from every local body so the secondary body-equality skip cannot mask an inert primary skip.\n\nACs:\n- Recorded post skipped + unrecorded control still emits: DONE — test_recorded_post_is_skipped_and_unrecorded_control_still_emits.\n- Inert-guard variant re-emits: DONE — test_inert_is_comment_mapped_reemits_the_recorded_comment (instance-level is_comment_mapped forced False → recorded comment re-emits).\n- Discriminating power proven RED-first: hard-wiring the store guard False failed the seam test; probe removed before commit.\n\nGates: 2/2 tests pass; make lint (ruff + format + complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0); make typecheck clean; full CI Verified+1 across py3.11-3.13 ubuntu + macos.","timestamp":1787467719437178001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787397437256325001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"866ef06e-cf8d-408b-9048-ecc7e5d53327","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"2399-5e49-6b28-4d59"},{"link_uuid":"ac82a546-5830-43d0-b9dd-ad810c679441","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"00e2-6216-1085-4991"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nFiled from the escape analysis on marshy-chummy-coot (2399-5e49-6b28-4d59). An instrumented\nrun (a pytest plugin hard-wiring `BindingStore.is_comment_mapped` to `False` on every loaded\nmodule copy) showed the dedup suite could not observe the primary skip being disabled\nend-to-end: the differ tests seed map state via a private `_StubBindingStore`\n(`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_comment_id_map_diff.py`), while the apply tests\nseed synthetic id-bearing payloads. Each layer's test seeds the invariant the other layer is\nsupposed to establish; no single test crosses the apply-to-differ seam with a control that\nproves the assertion actually depends on `is_comment_mapped`.\n\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_id_acli_envelope.py` (fix 8d98c298fa8) got\nclose — its `test_no_reemission_after_an_acli_post_even_when_the_body_diverges` posts the real\nenvelope, records, and re-diffs one store — but it has no unrecorded-control variant and no\ninert-guard variant, so a hard-wired-False `is_comment_mapped` still cannot be distinguished\nfrom a store that was never written.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd one new test module,\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_dedup_seam_crossing.py` (test-only; no\nproduction code), that drives the WHOLE seam with a real `BindingStore` instance:\n\n1. Reuse the recorded envelope: `from .test_comment_id_acli_envelope import\n   ACLI_SUCCESS_ENVELOPE` (relative test-package imports are the established pattern —\n   `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_backend_capability.py:20` does `from .backend_support\n   import ...`) and obtain the transport return by calling the REAL\n   `acli_cli_ops.add_comment` stubbed only at the `acli_subprocess._run_acli` seam, exactly\n   as that module's `acli_result` fixture does.\n2. Seam test: a ticket carries TWO local comments (K_posted, K_control). First\n   `_diff_comments(ticket, key, remote, binding_store=store)`\n   (`rebar_reconciler.outbound_comments._diff_comments`) emits both. Simulate the apply for\n   K_posted only via the real `dispatch_apply_phases._record_comment_id(store, entry,\n   result)`. Re-diff against the SAME store: assert K_posted is absent and K_control is\n   still emitted. The Jira-side body diverges from both local bodies, so the SECONDARY\n   body-equality skip cannot mask an inert PRIMARY id-identity skip.\n3. Inert-guard variant (encodes the \"verify by temporarily disabling the guard\" check\n   durably): monkeypatch the store instance's `is_comment_mapped` to always return `False`\n   and assert the re-diff RE-EMITS K_posted — proving the seam assertion discriminates on\n   the guard rather than passing vacuously.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_dedup_seam_crossing.py` — new test module\n  (the only change; non-goal reaffirmed: no production code, no new review criterion).\n\n## Testing\n\nThe change IS tests: happy path (recorded comment skipped on re-diff), control path\n(unrecorded comment still emitted from the same store/ticket), and the inert-guard failure\npath (forcing `is_comment_mapped` to `False` re-emits the recorded comment). During\ndevelopment the discriminating power is additionally verified RED-first by running the seam\ntest with the guard temporarily disabled and observing the failure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A test posts via the real recording path (`_record_comment_id`) with the real envelope\n      fixture (obtained through the real `acli_cli_ops.add_comment`, stubbed only at\n      `_run_acli`) against a real `BindingStore`, then re-diffs with `_diff_comments` against\n      that SAME store instance — checked by\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_dedup_seam_crossing.py`.\n- [x] The re-diff asserts the skip engages for the recorded comment AND does not engage for\n      an unrecorded control comment — checked by the same pytest run.\n- [x] The suite fails if `is_comment_mapped` is inert: a variant forcing it to `False`\n      asserts the recorded comment is re-emitted — checked by the same pytest run.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_dedup_seam_crossing.py","reason":"new seam-crossing dedup test module (test-only change)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","00e2-6216-1085-4991"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"4c591fa8-4a3a-4dec-a86f-9ef0fefe6d46","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9dc3-7d6c-83d7-41c7","ticket_type":"task","title":"Seam-crossing dedup test: real envelope through record then re-diff same store","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f6d15835-51ab-4f9b-ae58-24863fa97f15","7b64447c-1f65-4083-9ed4-a064742f464c","a2eb0ece-e552-4f7d-a277-18a6eedec0ef","535cbf20-9cc7-4084-b9c8-eba9a6dac7bb","dbcd4ef1-d37a-4924-ab95-8a2a360f3de7","ac82a546-5830-43d0-b9dd-ad810c679441","7ec1dfea-de75-4dd8-a1e2-cb0bced42e8e","1faaf35b-3e6e-4032-9884-c0229ea07d5a","5a77e082-1cb5-474c-af4d-22078366cc2c","4c591fa8-4a3a-4dec-a86f-9ef0fefe6d46","bf3642f0-4407-46f5-a01f-7dceb3d9e2c3"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787473998835076001,"uuid":"60b3cf67-6d58-49cf-8519-3ec203332b03"}